Description:

The IMAP APPEND command's CATENATE extension now counts the size of TEXT and
UTF8 parts toward the running total for the message being assembled.
Previously that total was never advanced for those parts, so each TEXT or
UTF8 part was measured against the entire :imapdconf:`maxmessagesize` budget
rather than against whatever remained of it.  An authenticated user with
permission to append to a mailbox could therefore use CATENATE to assemble a
message of any size out of individually acceptable pieces, exceeding both the
configured limit and the APPENDLIMIT value the server advertises.  URL parts
were always counted correctly and were not affected.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-prx2-vhpq-ph9j.


